            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. CompletableFuture",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> x, pool)",
                "  .thenApply(f)",
                "  .thenCompose(g)",
                "  .thenCombine(other, fn)",
                "  .exceptionally(ex -> dflt);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`thenApply` = map; `thenCompose` = flatMap, flattens a returned future",
                "No executor → ==commonPool==; pass your own for blocking IO",
                "`allOf` waits for all; `anyOf` first to finish"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why no null?** `get()` returning null is ambiguous: absent key or null value?",
                "**thenApply vs thenCompose?** Map a value vs flatten a returned future.",
                "**Exceptions?** `exceptionally`, `handle` or `whenComplete` in the chain.",
                "**Why computeIfAbsent?** Check and put run as one atomic step."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
